<spell-notebook "root examples">
	<header level="1">
		Root
		<header>A root loads the components inside it on demand, sets their theme, size, icons and emoji, and shows
              them once they're ready.</>
	</>
	<root-tab-bar showing="examples"/>
	<section>
		<html>
			<ui-menu class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
				<ui-item link="#types">Types</>
				<ui-item link="#while-loading">While loading</>
				<ui-item link="#icons-and-emoji">Icons and emoji</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<!--
		EXAMPLES:  ours only, no Fomantic page.  The old Astro page's examples, restyled.  This page itself runs inside a
		`<ui-root display="immediately">`, which loads every example's components;  the roots below are NESTED in it.
		- Icon packs:  the page's root already has every built-in pack, so the icon examples use a pack of their own,
		  `site/examples/icon-pack/` (one icon, `spell sparkle`).
		- The Replay example needs the small script at the end of this tab:  components on this page are loaded already.
	-->
	<section label="Types">
		<section label="Root" sticky collapsible dividing>
			<example description="Put one around a page or an app:  each `ui-*` tag inside loads its component the first time it appears, and nothing else is downloaded. Load just the root: `import \"spell/ui/ui-root\"`.">
				<html>
					<ui-root>
						<ui-segment>
							<ui-header>Report</ui-header>
							<p>Every component in here was loaded by the root, on demand.</p>
							<ui-button color="primary">Save</ui-button>
						</ui-segment>
					</ui-root>
				</html>
			</example>
		</>

		<section label="Theme and size" sticky collapsible dividing>
			<example description="`theme` and `size` apply to everything inside.">
				<html>
					<ui-root theme="dark" size="small" width="100%" aria-label="Dark report">
						<ui-segment>
							<ui-header>Report</ui-header>
							<p>Dark and small: everything inside follows.</p>
							<ui-button color="primary">Save</ui-button>
						</ui-segment>
					</ui-root>
				</html>
			</example>
		</>

		<section label="A box" sticky collapsible dividing>
			<example description="With `width` or `height` (CSS lengths, or `window` for the viewport's), the root is a box that scrolls its own content.  `fixed` pins it to the viewport:  a full-page app shell.">
				<root height="8em" aria-label="Numbers">
					<list bulleted>
						<item>One</item>
						<item>Two</item>
						<item>Three</item>
						<item>Four</item>
						<item>Five</item>
						<item>Six</item>
						<item>Seven</item>
						<item>Eight</item>
					</list>
				</root>
			</example>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="While loading">
		<markdown>
			`display` says what shows until every component inside is ready (or `timeout`, 5s by default, has passed):

			- `skeleton` (the default): a `<ui-placeholder>` for each component that describes one, drawn in the root's own
			  shadow DOM, so your page's DOM is never touched. Placeholders stack in page order; inline ones (buttons,
			  labels, inputs) sit side by side.
			- `when-ready`: nothing, with the space kept.
			- `immediately`: everything as it arrives.

			`loading="..."` shows a `<ui-loader>` with that message instead (a bare `loading` says "Loading…").
		</>

		<section label="Replay" sticky collapsible dividing>
			<example description="Components on this page are loaded already, so the demo holds the root for 2 seconds:  press a button to see what a slow load shows.">
				<button icon="redo" data-replay="skeleton">Replay: skeleton</button>
				<button icon="redo" data-replay="loading">Replay: loading message</button>
				<segment id="root-replay-stage" appearance="basic">
					<root display="skeleton">
						<card>
							<content>
								<header>Report</header>
								<description>Every component inside was ready before this showed.</description>
							</content>
						</card>
						<button color="primary">Save</button>
						<button>Cancel</button>
					</root>
				</segment>
			</example>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Icons and emoji">
		<section label="Icon packs" sticky collapsible dividing>
			<example description="`icons` adds packs for everything inside, comma-separated, later wins:  built-in ids (fa7-free, fa7-brands, fomantic) or `pack.js` URLs. Outside a root, the page's packs apply (`UI.icons.use()`):  the sparkle is only in the example's own pack, so inside the root it draws, outside it doesn't.">
				<html>
					<p>Inside: <ui-root icons="examples/icon-pack/pack.js" display="immediately"><ui-icon name="spell sparkle" size="big" label="Sparkle"></ui-icon></ui-root> Outside: <ui-icon name="spell sparkle" size="big" label="Sparkle"></ui-icon></p>
				</html>
			</example>
		</>

		<section label="Emoji names" sticky collapsible dividing>
			<example description="`emoji=\"fomantic\"` uses Fomantic's names for everything inside;  outside, the page's set (CLDR by default).  `pencil` is a memo in Fomantic's names, a pencil in CLDR's.">
				<html>
					<p>Inside: <ui-root emoji="fomantic" display="immediately"><ui-emoji name="pencil" size="small" label="pencil (Fomantic)"></ui-emoji></ui-root> Outside: <ui-emoji name="pencil" size="small" label="pencil (CLDR)"></ui-emoji></p>
				</html>
			</example>
		</>

		<!-- GAP I62:  a root's `size` scales only components (its scale token), not plain text or a bare `<ui-icon>` inside. -->
		<section label="Nested roots" sticky collapsible dividing>
			<example description="A root inside a root inherits what it doesn't set and adds its own packs.  The outer one is ready only once every inner one is.">
				<root icons="examples/icon-pack/pack.js" display="immediately">
					<button icon="spell sparkle">Outer</button>
					<root size="large" display="immediately">
						<button icon="spell sparkle">Inner: large, with the outer root's pack</button>
					</root>
				</root>
			</example>
		</>
	</>
</spell-notebook>
